## 2026-09-30 18:22 UTC governance017-004 ran once and failed on the delta-file 400-line cap

After the owner freed space (D: 299,857,735,680 free at 18:21:35 UTC,
gate passed with large margin) and a fresh full guard sweep passed
(worktrees exact, helper hashes pinned, create-once paths absent, owner
window valid), governance017-004 ran **once** at 18:22 UTC and exited 1
after 2.2 seconds. Evidence: create-once start receipt
`doc-governance-017-proposal015-started.json` and failure receipt
`doc-governance-017-proposal015-failed.json` (start SHA256
`9c8112732ccb669e0edb9afba9477d8a66438580d8e2aa6a42cb5d3672595e84`);
QA root `r30-doc-governance-017` with junit/stdout/result/command;
scratch `.tmp/r12-r30-doc-governance-017` (empty). No finish receipt.
Source unchanged (exactly nine dirty files remain; candidate
before/after manifests equal). **Never replay governance017-004.**

Cause: `tests/test_project_state.py::test_delta_file_is_pasteable`
failed — DELTA_TO_SOL.md has 409 lines against its 400-line cap
(`--maxfail=1` stopped the suite at 11 of 14 cases; 10 passed). The
file was already at exactly 400 lines at the D-174 parent commit; the
proposal014/015 documentation apply appended the 9-line DELTA_ID: 83
block, pushing it 9 over. This is the same cap-defect class as
governance016's PROJECT_STATE.md 506>500, on the delta channel.

Analysis: the decisions ledger records the established precedent for a
full delta channel (DECISIONS.md, delta39–42 era): when the 400-line cap
is reached with undelivered deltas, new content rides the complete git
diff carried by the bundle and a dedicated delta joins the next batch
after delivery — do not cram past the cap. DELTA_ID: 83 was appended
against that precedent. Machine-check analysis of all 14 tests shows
that removing the delta83 block returns the file to its exact D-174
bytes (400 lines, no longer dirty) while every doc-governance test
passes: PROJECT_STATE.md's session log lists only the 2026-09-27
session, which delta82's COVERS SESSIONS already names; no other dirty
doc references delta 83; identifiers/chain/flag checks remain green.
Remediation therefore follows the proposal014→015 pattern: a distinct
proposal016 docs correction (revert the delta83 block), new 263-file
manifest, admission010 and governance017-005 successors, then re-staged
runtime/residue/inspection/commit successors. No replay of any consumed
helper. The alternative — delivering deltas 64–83 to Sol now — is an
external action outside the current local/private window.

