## 2026-10-01 06:40 UTC attempt011 renderer -001 refused on owner-record UTF-8 decoding; -002 successor staged

The bound renderer -001 (`0f688d77...`, reviewed PASS) ran once at ~06:25
UTC during a transient quiet-host gap and refused pre-artifact at its
owner-lineage check: NOTHING was consumed (attempt011 absent, no receipt).
Root cause, isolated empirically: the Oct2 owner record
(OWNER_D175_WINDOW_OCT02_EXTENSION_001.json) is BOM-less UTF-8 carrying
U+2013 in its question field (bytes 199-201; it is the ONLY evidence file
with non-ASCII bytes); Windows PowerShell 5.1 `Get-Content -Raw` without
-Encoding decodes it as Windows-1252, so the exact-string comparison
fails. This is the same encoding false-alarm class the earlier session
documented in AGENTS.md (2026-09-30 12:20 UTC) — the Oct2 template family
shipped with the latent runtime defect because static reviews read the
files as UTF-8 themselves.

The -002 successor is staged: all seven JSON reads now use
`-Encoding UTF8`, plus a three-line docstring note; same twelve
proposal016 bindings as -001. Template `406b43c8...`, bound
`bf10d942cabec584cef913d86ebf3a32f35ca4ddefa1711d26bdd9979beedd69`; both
parse-clean; layered diffs mechanically exact (17 then 24 changed lines);
delta review in flight. -001 is preserved as a terminal pre-artifact
refusal; never replay it. The same `Get-Content -Raw` pattern exists in
the status transport (13 sites), adjudicate transport002 (9), poststatus
common (10) and postseal monitor common (12); encoding-fixed successors
of each will be staged before their bindings. The host quiet gap closed
(watchers respawn on ~minute cycles); durable quiet still requires the
owner to pause the pro3 job and the codex-runtimes parent session.

Correction (07:05 UTC): the delta review of renderer -002 proved the
encoding diagnosis INCOMPLETE for this refusal. The deterministic cause is
PowerShell case-insensitive variable shadowing: inside Assert-OwnerWindow
the parsed-record assignments `$owner0100`/`$owner2200` clobber the
script-scope path variables `$Owner0100`/`$Owner2200`, so
`GetFileName($Owner0100)` receives the PSCustomObject dump, not the
filename — three lineage clauses fail identically in -001 and -002. The
U+2013 mis-decode is real but latent (the only affected field compared is
oct01.question, pure ASCII). A -003 successor (variable rename + retained
UTF-8 reads + same bindings) is required; -002 is preserved unrun. The
same collision pattern must be audited across the sibling Oct2 templates
before binding them.

